failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for the sole managed node: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the restart, observed a changed boot ID, and demonstrated recovered system, SSH, filesystem, retained data, writable-directory behavior, and sticky-bit enforcement. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor observations.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector did not independently inspect /srv/drop, so its final task-specific state is established by direct executor commands rather than a separate global probe.","Package-health observations timed out both before and after execution, limiting independent package-consistency assurance; however, the command timeline contains no package-management mutations.","Seven small verification/reboot files remained under /tmp, as detailed in the operational-hygiene assessment."]}
